"""The concept layer of the mind: what an investor needs to know, as a typed graph. Each concept has a plain definition
(our words), an optional formula, aliases a reader might type, and typed relations to other concepts, to measured
series (s:...), to engine modules (e:...) and to voices topics (t:...). mind.py joins this with the atlas, the engine,
the countries and the voices into one graph.

Relations: is_a, part_of, measures, causes+ (raises), causes- (lowers), uses, implemented_by, related, opposes,
example_of, priced_by, hedges. Weights are for activation (how strongly thinking about one recalls the other), not
causal sizes; causal sizes live in the atlas.
"""
